 The word "callous" is used to carry the connotation of "pragmatic" --
it's callous to say to yourself "I'm not running into that burning
building to save some stranger's baby! I might get killed!"
 In contrast, the word "cruel" is generally used for things like kicking
puppies, or knocking down a little old lady and laughing as she breaks her
hip. Cruel implies "mean" rather than just "heartless."

 IOW, Callous says 'he doesn't care if someone else suffers' whereas cruel
says 'he *likes* it when someone else suffers.' It's an active/passive
difference.


